( Rectangular Probing - PathPilot-safe version, rev 3.2                 )
(                                                                       )
( Probes a grid and logs each point as a G1 line, in the ACTIVE WCS.    )
(                                                                       )
( GEOMETRY - the grid starts at #1,#4 and runs POSITIVE:                )
(     X: #1 to #1 + #2*[#3-1]                                           )
(     Y: #4 to #4 + #5*[#6-1]                                           )
( Probes in the ACTIVE WCS. Placement is set by pcbmill solve-offsets,  )
( which measures the toolpath extents and centres them on the blank -   )
( nothing here needs to match any CAM tool's origin convention.         )
(                                                                       )
( Z SETUP - #7 is measured ABOVE the WCS Z zero; the machine must have  )
( that much Z+ travel left after you set that zero. #8 is the probe     )
( depth LIMIT: G38.2 aborts the program if it finds nothing by then.    )
(                                                                       )
( ZERO Z ON THE COPPER by electrical touch. A used MDF backer carries  )
( wax and never gives a true zero again. The map then holds the copper  )
( deviation from that zero, which applymap consumes in absolute mode;   )
( the board bottom is the blank thickness below. Set #8 below the       )
( copper by more than any bow.                                          )
(                                                                       )
( rev 3.3: flush the log at the end of every row. LOG output is only  )
(   committed when the file is closed, so an abort mid-run previously  )
(   lost EVERYTHING. LOGCLOSE + LOGAPPEND each row means you lose at   )
(   most one row. LOGOPEN truncates, LOGAPPEND preserves.              )
( rev 3.2: FIXES THE HANG AT EVERY ROW CHANGE.                          )
(   The serpentine turn makes the first X target of a new row equal to  )
(   the last X of the previous row, so G38.3 was a zero-length move.    )
(   PathPilot leaves #5070 stale at 1 for a null probe move, so #12     )
(   never cleared and the O4 loop spun forever with no motion.          )
(   #15 now holds the last completed X target and the traverse is       )
(   skipped when we are already there. #14 is a retry backstop.         )
( rev 3.1: un-nested the parens in these comments. NO nested parens!    )
( rev 1: #5070=1 replaced with local flag #12                           )
( rev 2/3: guarded the G38.5 back-off, contact state tracked in #13     )
(Configuration section)
G20   (Inches)
F10    (probe speed)
#1=.1    (X start)
#2=.2    (X increment)
#3=14    (X count)
#4=.1    (Y start)
#5=.2    (Y increment)
#6=20    (Y count)
#7=.25   (Z safety, above WCS Z0)
#8=-.05  (Z probe depth limit, below WCS Z0)
(SET UP FOR A 70x100mm PCB BLANK = 2.756 x 3.937 inch                  )
(  X0 Y0 must be the LOWER-LEFT CORNER of the blank, not its centre.   )
(  Grid runs 0.100 to 2.700 in X, 0.100 to 3.900 in Y - inset 0.1 from )
(  every edge so the stylus never hangs off the board. 280 points.     )
(End configuration section)
(Probe is T99 with length offset 99 - required by Tormach for probing)
G54
G43 H99
(Bare filename - lands in the PathPilot .ini directory. Find it with: )
(  find / -name probe-results.ngc -newermt today 2>/dev/null )
(LOGOPEN,probe-results.ngc)
#9=0 #10=0
#15=9999                         (last completed X - impossible start)
G0Z#7
#13=0                            (0 = probe known clear at safe Z)
O1 while [#9 lt #6]
    #10=0
    G0 Y[#4+#5*#9]
    O2 while [#10 lt #3]
        O3 if [[#9/2] - fix[#9/2] eq 0]
            #11=[#1+#2*#10]
        O3 else
            #11=[#1+#2*[#3-#10-1]]
        O3 endif
        (#11 is X target)
        #12=1                    (retry flag)
        #14=0                    (retry counter)
        O4 while [#12 NE 0]
            O5 if [#13 NE 0]
                G38.5 z#7        (back off, only if we may be in contact)
            O5 endif
            O6 if [ABS[#11 - #15] GT .0005]
                G38.3 x#11       (traverse to next X, stop if it touches)
                #12=#5070        (1 = tripped during traverse, retry)
            O6 else
                #12=0            (already at target - skip the null move)
            O6 endif
            #13=#12
            #14=[#14+1]
            O7 if [#14 GT 20]
                (DEBUG, smartprobe: X retry limit hit)
                #12=0
            O7 endif
        O4 endwhile
        #15=#11
        G38.2Z#8
        #13=1                    (probe is in contact with the surface)
        (LOG,G1 X#5061 Y#5062 Z#5063)
        #10=[#10+1]
    O2 endwhile
    G0Z#7
    #13=0
    #9=[#9+1]
    (LOGCLOSE)
    (LOGAPPEND,probe-results.ngc)
O1 endwhile
(LOGCLOSE)
G0Z#7
G0X#1Y#4
M2
